# Core §15 — A HOST-LANGUAGE NAME IS AN ORDINARY ID, under `sequence`.
#
# The sequence half of `960-prototype-names-as-ids`, experimental because the
# genre is. The sequence model keys its containers, their owned rows, its
# columns, its classes and its last-state table by author ids. Until
# 0.5 the reference engine kept those in plain objects:
# `fragment __proto__` with a member message threw, and `class=__proto__` on
# a message set a property on the prototype every later render in the
# process shares. Here each name is a fragment, an operand, a lifeline, a
# class and a state scope, and the document must parse and render like any
# other.
figdown 0.5 sequence
class __proto__ "retry path"
lifeline constructor "Client"
lifeline toString "Server"
fragment __proto__ "retry" type=loop
operand valueOf "until acknowledged" in=__proto__
message constructor -> toString "request" in=valueOf class=__proto__
state toString "WAIT" in=valueOf
message toString -> constructor "ack" in=valueOf
fragment hasOwnProperty "maybe" type=opt
message constructor -> toString "close" in=hasOwnProperty
